{"before_validation calls sub! on host unconditionally, which will raise NoMethodError when host is nil (e.g. missing params / blank input)": 0.9374092221260071, "In update action, if params[:id] doesn't match an existing record, host will be nil and save_host(host) will raise when it tries to assign attributes - should raise Discourse::NotFound when the record can't be found": 0.9793568849563599, "Migration inserts embeddable_hosts.host via raw string interpolation which is SQL-injection prone and bypasses the model's normalization (scheme/path/port stripping), causing EmbeddableHost.host_allowed? lookups to fail after the migration - should quote and normalize the host string before inserting": 0.9547576904296875, "spec/fabricators/category_fabricator.rb now defines the :embeddable_host fabricator while category fabricators live in spec/fabricators/embeddable_host_fabricator.rb - this inversion makes it hard to locate fabricators by filename - should swap these definitions so files match their primary fabricator": 0.8265727162361145, "Migration assumes the embed_category site_setting row exists and the join returns at least one row; if it doesn't, ...[0]['id'] will raise and the migration will fail - should handle an empty result set and only index into the PG result when rows exist": 0.9333627223968506, "In destroy action, if params[:id] doesn't match an existing record, host will be nil and host.destroy will raise - should return a 404 by raising Discourse::NotFound when the record can't be found": 0.9858801960945129, "Pretender handler ignores the requested :id and always returns fruits[0], making store.find('fruit', <id>) tests misleading - should select the fruit by request.params.id with a fallback if not found": 0.9756988286972046, "After making the Pretender /fruits/:id handler respect :id, the test should request the fruit that matches the expected color_ids assertions (currently those expectations match fruits[0], id 1)": 0.7848444581031799, "type.replace('_', '-') only replaces the first underscore - if an admin model type contains multiple underscores, it won't match ADMIN_MODELS and will incorrectly use the non-admin base path - should use a global replacement to normalize all underscores": 0.9481162428855896, "Typo in the describe block title: 'emeddable' should be 'embeddable'": 0.27235400676727295}